<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine taxmen seeking $6 billion in court cases.</title>
<headline>Argentine taxmen seeking $6 billion in court cases.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine government is pursuing court cases to recover tax payments totaling $6 billion, the head of the tax department said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;About half of the 400,000 court cases correspond to infractions of pension regulations,&quot; said tax chief Carlos Silvani.</p>
<p>He added that of the 17,000 largest businesses in the country, about 3,700 were being audited by the tax department.</p>
<p>((-- Patrick Adam, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0654))</p>
